      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A child with joint or extremity pain is a common presentation to the emergency department. Often, there is some element to the patient's history, whether it is trauma or some other significant history, which leads to a likely diagnosis. When there is a history of fever and progressive arm weakness, an astute emergency physician would have heightened awareness of a possible systemic process. We describe a case of unilateral shoulder pain with associated fever in a 7-year-old boy who presented to the emergency department with progressive arm weakness to the same side."},
